/*  Records — `TypeChecker.Records.cs`: a record written out, a field read or written by name, and
    the positional arms `InferSeriesAccess` and `CheckSeriesSet` give a record in
    `TypeChecker.Series.cs`.

    ★ A record TYPE is its shape, `(RecordType [<positional types>] [["name" <type>] …])`, with the
    named fields sorted by name — so two records are the same type whatever order their fields were
    written in, and `type-key` compares them as it compares anything else.
*/

Pull a book on collections.
    /// `a record with (…)` — its shape, read off the values.
    Bind node or failure to infer-record-literal unto checker, given (the node said):
        Define at-row as cast numeric on (cast field-of on (said, 3)).
        Define positional as cast listed.
        For each value in (cast field-of on (said, 1))'s children, repeat:
            Define value-type as cast one's infer on (value) or pass the failure off.
            If cast is-none on (value-type):
                Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("the type of a positional record field can't be determined", "",
                    at-row, "use an expression whose type can't be inferred as a record field",
                    "Start with a literal value or a defined variable so the field type is clear.")).
            Done.
            Cast positional's add on (value-type).
        Done.
        Define named as cast listed.
        Define seen as a map from text to fact.
        For each pair in (cast field-of on (said, 2))'s children, repeat:
            Define label as item 1 of pair's children.
            Define name as cast unquoted on (label).
            If (the entry for name in seen) is not void:
                Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("the record has two fields both named '{name}'", "",
                    at-row, "define a record with duplicate field name '{name}'", "Each named field must have a unique name.")).
            Done.
            In seen, the entry for name becomes true.
            Define value-type as cast one's infer on (item 2 of pair's children) or pass the failure off.
            If cast is-none on (value-type):
                Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("the type of field '{name}' can't be determined", "",
                    at-row, "use an expression whose type can't be inferred as a record field",
                    "Start with a literal value or a defined variable so the field type is clear.")).
            Done.
            Define field as cast listed.
            Cast field's add on (label).
            Cast field's add on (value-type).
            Cast named's add on (field).
        Done.
        Return cast made on ("RecordType", a series with (positional, cast sorted-by-name on (named))).
    Done.

    /// A record type's named field, or void.
    Bind voidable node to record-field-type, given (the node shape, the text name):
        For each pair in (cast field-of on (shape, 2))'s children, repeat:
            If cast unquoted on (item 1 of pair's children) is name, return item 2 of pair's children.
        Done.
        Return void.
    Done.

    Bind series of text to record-field-names, given (the node shape):
        Define names as a series of text.
        For each pair in (cast field-of on (shape, 2))'s children, repeat:
            Insert cast unquoted on (item 1 of pair's children) into names.
        Done.
        Return names.
    Done.

    /// `the <field> of <record>`, with the nearest field suggested when there is none by that name.
    Bind node or failure to record-field-access, given (the node shape, the text name, the number at-row):
        Define found as cast record-field-type on (shape, name).
        If found is not void, return found.
        Define names as cast record-field-names on (shape).
        // The nearest name within two edits, the first of the nearest when several tie.
        Define suggestion as "".
        Define nearest as 3.
        For each candidate in names, repeat:
            Define distance as cast edit-distance on (candidate, name).
            If distance is less than nearest:
                The suggestion becomes candidate.
                The nearest becomes distance.
            Done.
        Done.
        Define available as " This record has no named fields.".
        If the number of names is greater than 0:
            The available becomes " Named fields: {cast quoted-names on (names, "")}.".
        Done.
        Define fix as available.
        If suggestion is not "", the fix becomes "Did you mean '{suggestion}'?{available}".
        Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("this record has no field named '{name}'", "",
            at-row, "access field '{name}'", fix)).
    Done.

    /// `the <field> of <record> becomes …`.
    Bind void or failure to check-record-set unto checker, given (the node shape, the node statement):
        Define name as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (statement, 1)).
        Define at-row as cast numeric on (cast field-of on (statement, 4)).
        Define wanted as cast record-field-type on (shape, name).
        If wanted is void:
            Define names as cast record-field-names on (shape).
            Define fix as "This record has no named fields.".
            If the number of names is greater than 0:
                Define listing as a chase.
                Define first-one as true.
                For each field in names, repeat:
                    If first-one is false, insert ", " into listing.
                    The first-one becomes false.
                    Insert field into listing.
                Done.
                The fix becomes "Available named fields: {listing converted to text}.".
            Done.
            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("this record has no field named '{name}'", "",
                at-row, "set field '{name}'", fix)).
        Done.
        Define value as cast field-of on (statement, 3).
        Define value-type as cast one's infer on (value) or pass the failure off.
        If cast is-none on (value-type) is false and cast assignable on (wanted, value-type) is false:
            If cast beyond-types on (value-type), return a failure (cast not-judged on ("a {value-type's kind} in a field")).
            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("field '{name}' holds a {cast type-words on (wanted)}, not a {cast type-words on (value-type)}", "",
                at-row, "set field '{name}' to a {cast type-words on (value-type)}",
                "Field '{name}' has type {cast type-words on (wanted)}.")).
        Done.
        Cast one's check-region-store on (value, value-type, cast one's container-depth on (cast field-of on (statement, 2)), at-row,
            "set field '{name}' to a value from a shorter-lived region") or pass the failure off.
    Done.

    /// `item N of <record>` — its Nth positional field; a position that is not written out is
    /// only known when the program runs.
    Bind node or failure to record-item, given (the node shape, the node target, the node index-said, the number at-row):
        If cast is-nothing on (index-said):
            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("'last' doesn't work on records", "", at-row,
                "use 'last' on a record", "Use a position like 'the first of ...' or a field name like 'the city of ...'.")).
        Done.
        If index-said's kind is not "NumberLiteral", return cast unknown-type.
        Define positionals as (cast field-of on (shape, 1))'s children.
        Define spot as cast numeric on (cast field-of on (index-said, 1)).
        // C# truncates toward zero, as a cast to int does.
        Define whole as spot - (spot % 1).
        If whole is less than 1 or whole is greater than the number of positionals:
            Define shown as "this record".
            If target's kind is "VariableReference", the shown becomes "'{cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (target, 1))}'".
            Define said as "{shown} has {the number of positionals} positional field(s) — there is no position {whole}".
            Define fix as "Positions run 1 through {the number of positionals}.".
            If the number of positionals is 0:
                The said becomes "{shown} has no positional fields".
                The fix becomes "This record has no positional fields. Access fields by name instead.".
            Done.
            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on (said, "", at-row, "access position {whole}", fix)).
        Done.
        Return item whole of positionals.
    Done.

    /// `item N of <record> becomes …` — the value has to be exactly the field's type.
    Bind void or failure to check-record-item-set unto checker, given (the node shape, the node statement):
        Define target as cast field-of on (statement, 1).
        Define index-said as cast field-of on (statement, 2).
        Define at-row as cast numeric on (cast field-of on (statement, 4)).
        If cast is-nothing on (index-said):
            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("'last' doesn't work on records", "", at-row,
                "use 'last' on a record", "Use a position like 'the first of ...' or a field name like 'the city of ...'.")).
        Done.
        If index-said's kind is not "NumberLiteral", return.
        Define spoken as cast expression-words on (target).
        Define positionals as (cast field-of on (shape, 1))'s children.
        Define spot as cast numeric on (cast field-of on (index-said, 1)).
        Define whole as spot - (spot % 1).
        If whole is less than 1 or whole is greater than the number of positionals:
            Define said as "{spoken} has {the number of positionals} positional field(s) — there is no position {whole}".
            Define fix as "Positions run 1 through {the number of positionals}.".
            If the number of positionals is 0:
                The said becomes "{spoken} has no positional fields".
                The fix becomes "This record has no positional fields.".
            Done.
            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on (said, "", at-row, "set position {whole}", fix)).
        Done.
        Define wanted as item whole of positionals.
        Define given-type as cast one's infer on (cast field-of on (statement, 3)) or pass the failure off.
        If cast is-none on (given-type) is false and cast same-type on (given-type, wanted) is false:
            If cast beyond-types on (given-type), return a failure (cast not-judged on ("setting a position to a {given-type's kind}")).
            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on (
                "position {whole} of {spoken} holds a {cast type-words on (wanted)}, not a {cast type-words on (given-type)}", "",
                at-row, "set position {whole} to a {cast type-words on (given-type)}",
                "Position {whole} has type {cast type-words on (wanted)}.")).
        Done.
    Done.

    /// The edits — insert, delete or change one character — between two names. C#'s `Levenshtein`.
    Bind number to edit-distance, given (the text first, the text second):
        Define first-letters as a chase.
        Insert first into first-letters.
        Define second-letters as a chase.
        Insert second into second-letters.
        Define width as the number of second-letters.
        // One row of the table at a time: `above` is the row before, `current` the one being filled.
        Define above as a series of numbers.
        Define across as 0.
        While across is less than width + 1, repeat:
            Insert across into above.
            Increment across by 1.
        Done.
        Define down as 1.
        While down is less than (the number of first-letters) + 1, repeat:
            Define current as a series with (down).
            Define along as 1.
            While along is less than width + 1, repeat:
                Define best as (item (along + 1) of above) + 1.
                If (item along of current) + 1 is less than best, the best becomes (item along of current) + 1.
                Define diagonal as item along of above.
                If item down of first-letters is not item along of second-letters, the diagonal becomes diagonal + 1.
                If diagonal is less than best, the best becomes diagonal.
                Insert best into current.
                Increment along by 1.
            Done.
            The above becomes current.
            Increment down by 1.
        Done.
        Return item (width + 1) of above.
    Done.
Done.
